      "title": "DNA Day 2025: Where we are in the T2T Genomes Era, Pt 1",
      "abstract": "<jats:p>Today is International DNA Day, commemorating the day in 1953 when Crick, Watson, Wilkins and Franklin published their papers on the structure of DNA. Fifty years later, with the declaration that the human genome project was close to completion the US Senate and the House of Representatives declared that 25 &lt;sup&gt; th &lt;/sup&gt; April 2003 would be the first DNA Day, and ever since many (including ourselves through many blogs) have commemorated the date.</jats:p>",
